---
import DirectoryLayout from "../layouts/DirectoryLayout.astro";
import VerificationBadge from "../components/VerificationBadge.astro";
---

<DirectoryLayout
  heading="How We Verify Listings"
  subheading="A transparent breakdown of our verification tiers and what each badge means."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", item: "/" },
    { name: "How We Verify", item: "/how-we-verify" },
  ]}
  canonicalPath="/how-we-verify"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Our Core Verification Principle</h2>
      <p>
        Unlike many directories that generate fake "Verified" checkmarks to create an illusion of trust, our directory utilizes strictly defined verification states. We never use the word "Verified" without concrete evidence.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <!-- Unverified -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">1. Unverified</h3>
          <VerificationBadge status="unverified" />
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
          The public invite link was discovered through automated search or indexing, but no direct confirmation has been performed with an official primary domain or community owner.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Source Confirmed -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">2. Source Confirmed</h3>
          <VerificationBadge status="source-confirmed" />
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
          The invite link was linked directly from an official, authoritative website (e.g. project homepage, GitHub repository, official docs) confirming genuine community association.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Owner Confirmed -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">3. Owner Confirmed</h3>
          <VerificationBadge status="owner-confirmed" />
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
          The community founder or recognized administrator submitted verifiable proof of ownership and controls the listing details.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Manually Reviewed -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">4. Manually Reviewed</h3>
          <VerificationBadge status="manually-reviewed" />
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
          A human moderator independently inspected the link, title, categorization, and public activity to confirm basic legitimacy and absence of obvious spam.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Clear Scope Limitation -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/70 p-6 text-xs sm:text-sm text-amber-900 space-y-2">
      <strong class="font-bold text-amber-950 block">Important Safety Limitation</strong>
      <p>
        Verification of identity or source is NOT a guarantee of ongoing security, safety, or financial returns. Group ownership can change, and malicious actors can compromise accounts. Users must always maintain personal vigilance.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DirectoryLayout>
